Generate properly the markdown help

The info property is changed into a QVariant, so that more information can be set.
. For controls: if it is a string, this is as before just the text of the info. It can be used as an object like this: { text: "....", label: "....", useControlType: true, isHeader: true}
In this way the developer can specify whether the label can have another value than the title, whether the type of the control should be displayed and whether the info should be displayed as an header.

For Form, the info can be also just a string but also an object:
{ top: "..",, bottom: "...", references: ["ref1, "ref2"], RPackages: ["pack1", "pack2"], examples: ["example1", "example2"] }

make sure that decoding columnnames for jaspTable does not accidentally include square brackets []

Fixes https://github.com/jasp-stats/jasp-issues/issues/2625 where square brackets in columnnames mess up the table, because we use it for subcolumns
it is easily fixed however by specifically replacing [] by html entity codes &#x5B; and &#x5D;
